flowchart LR
  ATT[External Attacker]

  subgraph Z0[Untrusted Network]
    U[User/Admin Browsers]
    AG[Agents]
  end

  subgraph Z1[Edge Trust Boundary]
    T[Traefik]
  end

  subgraph Z2[Keywarden Trusted Zone]
    N[Nginx]
    APP[Keywarden App]
    DB[(PostgreSQL)]
    R[(Redis/Valkey)]
    CA[(CA Private Keys)]
  end

  subgraph Z3[Managed Host Zone]
    SSH[sshd + local accounts]
  end

  U -->|HTTPS| T -->|HTTPS| N --> APP
  AG -->|HTTPS/mTLS path| T
  AG --> SSH
  APP --> DB
  APP --> R
  APP --> CA

  ATT -.credential theft / token misuse.-> T
  ATT -.injection / auth bypass attempts.-> APP
  ATT -.MITM if proxy TLS/mTLS misconfigured.-> N
  ATT -.host compromise impact.-> SSH

  Note1[Key Risk: CA private keys are central high-value assets]
  CA --- Note1
